    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, my realtor just mentioned something about needing to set up an escrow account for my house purchase here in Toronto. I've never dealt with this before, can you explain what escrow actually is and why it's used during the closing process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! An escrow account is a neutral, third‑party hold on funds (or documents) that keeps the buyer’s money safe until all the conditions of the sale are met. In a Toronto home purchase, the lawyer or title‑insurance company will hold the deposit, mortgage money, and any adjustments, then release them when the title transfers, taxes are paid, and any other contract terms are satisfied. This protects both buyer and seller by making sure no one can access the money until the deal is officially closed.",
