    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "gotcha. so it's basically a way to make sure nothing \"sneaks\" through or gets lost in the shuffle during the handoff. sounds like a lot of responsibility for that third party to have, like they're guarding everything.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's right—escrow agents (usually lawyers, notaries, or title‑insurance companies) are legally obligated to follow strict rules, keep detailed records, and only release funds when every contractual condition is met. Because they’re regulated professionals, any mishandling can lead to legal liability, professional sanctions, or malpractice claims, which gives you added protection that a private “hand‑off” wouldn’t provide.",
      "source": "target",
